<title>DENMARK: Danish November unemployment falls to 8.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish November unemployment falls to 8.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 8.2 percent of the workforce in November 1996, down from 8.3 percent in October, the National Statistics Office said on Monday.  </p>
<p>    DANISH UNEMPLOYMENT Nov 1996    Oct 1996   Nov 1995</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate    8.2 pct     8.3 pct    9.6 pct*</p>
<p>    Total unemployed     228,700    232,800*    267,300*</p>
<p>*Revised</p>
<p>NOTE - All above figures seasonally adjusted. A panel of economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast November unemployment of 8.25 percent.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650.</p>
</text>
